# a5sf-p2-read — RED capture (BL-14 / P2-01, dated 2026-11-03, real UTC; round 2)

Host-free. No boot, no port, no DSH_HOME, no budget row. This is the capture of the
tests BEFORE the package's laws could hold — not a re-run of the green state.

ROUND 2 NOTE (review C7/C3/C4). The first round's capture is superseded here because
the module changed. Two things are different from a naive capture:

  * the raw blocks are the real command output, but blank lines inside the node:test
    assertion diffs that contained only spaces were trimmed to empty lines so
    `git diff --check` is clean (review C7). Nothing else in the output was edited.
  * two NEW mutations (M3, M4) cover the two laws this round added (review C3, C4).

Five RED measurements, all real command output:

  RED 1  the gate's module does not exist (the file this package adds) — the
         "no gate at all" baseline: every arm red with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND.
  RED 2  M1: the FOREIGN-COMMIT comparison is deleted.
  RED 3  M2: the whole pre-reservation CAPACITY block is deleted.
  RED 4  M3: only the REMAINING-capacity disjunct is deleted (C3).
  RED 5  M4: the non-native NOT_REACHED branch of windowCaseVerdict() is deleted (C4).

Method: each mutation was applied to tests/world-factory/suites/150-a5sf-read.mjs, the
C1 suite was run, the module was restored from a saved copy. `orig sha` and `restored
sha` below must both equal the module's sha256 as shipped after this round's last edit
(387c657b61a9648e7d7dd942b0504dd0a84a88e03f8bb8d7166857d95943fba5); a capture is worthless if the file it measured is not the file shipped.

Mutation table (what was deleted -> which arm must red -> observed):

  M1  the `GRANT_FOREIGN_COMMIT` comparison
      -> arm 4 "a grant bound to ANOTHER commit refuses"                -> RED 1 failed
  M2  the whole pre-reservation capacity block
      -> arm 6 "an EXHAUSTED shared ledger refuses …" AND
         arm 6b "a PARTIALLY-SPENT pool refuses BEFORE reserving"       -> RED 2 failed
  M3  only `before.remaining < INTENT_ROWS_PER_LEASE + requiredBoots`
      -> arm 6b ONLY (the `exhausted` half still covers arm 6)          -> RED 1 failed
  M4  `if (native !== true) return NOT_REACHED …` in windowCaseVerdict
      -> the pure-function arm AND the dry-scene test (which asserts the
         dry run records the window case NOT_REACHED)                   -> RED 2 failed

Every mutation left the other arms green: the suite fails for the deleted law, not
because a file was broken.

